; Loose-CBOR `any` positions: every position that lowers CDDL `any` to the AnyCbor static-runtime
; type. Snapshotted under default / preserve / preserve+canonical / json by the `whole_program`
; suite (all `--wasm=false`, since a wasm crate is not a source snapshot). `any` is a full-surface
; citizen — the wasm AnyCbor wrapper means the `--wasm=true` leg is
; swept by the corpus axis of `wasm_api_parity`, and the JSON flags by the `any_positions_json`
; snapshot leg.
;
; Non-choice positions: member value, array element, table domain/range, top-level alias, tag.
; Type-choice-arm positions: a BARE `any` catch-all in LAST position (forced-backtracking
; dispatch — a typed arm matching on wire type but failing on content falls through to `any`), and a
; TAGGED `any` arm (`#6.n(any)`, cbor_types = [Tag]) which type-dispatches like any tagged arm and so
; is allowed in any position.
member_map = {1: any, ? 2: uint}   ; struct-map member value
member_array = [any, uint]         ; array-record member value
homog_array = [* any]              ; homogeneous array element
table_any_any = {* any => any}     ; table domain AND range
table_uint_any = {* uint => any}   ; table range
table_any_uint = {* any => uint}   ; table domain
top_alias = any                    ; top-level alias
tagged = #6.11(any)                ; tagged
choice_last_any = uint / tstr / any ; type-choice with a bare `any` catch-all arm (last position)
choice_tagged_any = #6.11(any) / tstr ; tagged-`any` type-choice arm (any position; not a catch-all)
;
; Collection-of-`any` MEMBER positions (natural-JSON rendering): a struct field
; whose value is a homogeneous `[* any]` array (the `Seq` natural adapter) or a `{* K => any}` table
; with a stringifiable key (the `Map` natural adapter — non-preserve; a preserve-mode map member keeps
; the tagged element rendering pending the `OrderedHashMap` adapter). Unlike a STANDALONE table/array
; alias (which has no generated JSON surface of its own), these members DO serialize, so their `any`
; content must render naturally element-wise.
member_homog = {1: uint, 2: [* any]}   ; homogeneous-array member value → Seq natural adapter
member_table = {1: uint, 2: {* uint => any}} ; table-range member → Map (non-preserve) / OrderedMap (preserve)
member_opt_homog = {1: uint, ? 2: [* any]}      ; optional homog-array member → OptSeq natural adapter
member_opt_table = {1: uint, ? 2: {* uint => any}} ; optional table member → OptMap / OptOrderedMap adapter
